  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Maven now requires you to use HTTPS when downloading packages, but for the KarafIT tests in fcrepo-camel and fcrepo-camel-toolbox the old PaxExam still uses non-SSL connections which fail.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "See the ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://github.com/Islandora/documentation/issues/1443"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "issue in Islandora",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " that revealed this issue to me.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This needs the 4.14.0 release of PaxExam which is not yet released.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "To replicate, delete your local maven repository (~/.m2/repository in Mac or Linux) and build fcrepo-camel.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": " ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "See",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
